# PE1: shadow obligation journal

This pilot retains eight Kernel obligations across edits. It records which archived evidence still authorizes an exact revision, which alternatives survive, and which work remains owed. The existing judge and source gates remain authoritative. The Kernel sources and landed theorem statements are unchanged.

## Components and boundary

- Lang/Contextual/Journal.lean defines immutable revisions, receipts, history and the finite Closure adapter. Receipt checking compares data: exact revision, checked result, completeness, and declared input versions. It never invokes Lean.
- Lang/Proofs/Contextual/Journal.lean proves revision correspondence, successful receipt admission, finite support locality, Protocol repair, sequential/batch composition and history preservation. JournalTeeth gives inhabited positive and negative instances.
- Census/JournalExpr.lean serializes the actual Expr/Level/Name graph, preserving numeric names, universe levels, projection structures and shared nodes.
- Census/Journal.lean exports transitive type, value and structural dependencies, axiom sets and syntactic local-premise applications. It separately rechecks saved proof terms with the kernel against current declaration types. Current support declarations that disappear are recorded as unavailable, never silently omitted.
- Census/JournalRun.lean runs the landed Closure.judge on finite receipt JSON and exercises the landed Worlds analysis.
- gates/journal.py validates complete exports, maintains a derived inverted index and appends a locked, hash-chained journal. The list scan is the reference oracle.
- gates/journal_pilot.py runs each scratch edit from the same checked baseline, retaining whole outputs. journal_compose.py checks sequential/full/batch observations on the same archived candidates.
- journal_plants.py, journal_coverage_plants.py and journal_finish.py contain real disabling plants and final receipt-boundary checks.

The proved boundary is finite receipt data, not exporter correctness, SHA-256 collision resistance, arbitrary Lean audit completeness or external process authenticity. A successful receipt is authorized only after the recorded external execution succeeds with complete inventory. Hashes are engineering version identifiers; the theorems use exact string equality and do not turn hash equality into semantic equality.

The Protocol fragment theorem concerns finite receipt-check/input observations. Full Closure verdicts, policy tokens and residual equality are additionally exercised by the executable oracle comparisons. No theorem here equates newly discovered candidate sets, proof search histories or selected proof terms. Candidate identity includes the entire archived receipt, supports, blockers and cost and is checked beside every runtime repair equality.

## Revisions and evidence

A revision identifies the claim, full target, universe context, transitive contract definitions, deployment-instance label and toolchain. Contract identity omits theorem proof bodies; receipt inputs retain the full proof dependency closure. Hence replacing a support proof under the same contract leaves the obligation revision unchanged but can invalidate an old receipt.

Two archived routes per obligation share a checked artifact: retained-term evidence and independently successful recipe reconstruction. Their support tokens are distinct. Recipe receipts additionally depend on a conservative hash of the source import closure, lakefile, toolchain and explicit attribute input. This deliberately over-invalidates recipe evidence after an irrelevant module edit. It does not claim that the proof became false.

A receipt carries its explicit result: checked, rejected, exhausted or incomplete. Timeout/resource failure is unavailable evidence. It is never a Boolean counterexample to the target. The journal retains old events and eight persistent obligations through incomplete coverage. Its hash chain detects accidental/tampered history with a retained head; it is not an authenticated publication ledger or a proof against a complete rewritten chain.

The semantic audit detects the tested outer global-hash existential escape. Other statement shapes require separate semantic review. In the scratch escape, a Bool-valued digest has a collision among three explicit byte arrays; the escaped disjunct follows from the instance alone. A newly checked literal theorem can therefore coexist with a pruning reason for the advertised binding obligation.

## Running on the designated build host

Use an owned warm worktree and a fresh lane scratch directory for each independent run. Set CARGO_TARGET_DIR to that worktree's target. All execution is constrained to 6G/two threads; Lean invocations in the harness have explicit finite heartbeats. The 800000 allocation budget for each kernel replay is added to the current absolute heartbeat count.

Scoped build:
    SWARM_MEM_MAX=6G LEAN_NUM_THREADS=2 swarm-build lake build Census.JournalRun Lang.Proofs.Contextual.JournalTeeth

Fresh matrix:
    SWARM_MEM_MAX=6G LEAN_NUM_THREADS=2 swarm-build python3 gates/journal_pilot.py --out /tank/dregg-build/nanodregg/logs/CX-PE1-fresh

Journal replay:
    SWARM_MEM_MAX=6G LEAN_NUM_THREADS=2 swarm-build python3 gates/journal.py inspect /tank/dregg-build/nanodregg/logs/CX-PE1-fresh/events.jsonl

The matrix needs only its owned scratch sources and read-only symlinks to its own worktree's warm artifacts. It does not copy a .lake, alter Kernel files, run cargo suites, or land anything. --resume validates source, recipe inputs and prior output hashes before reusing completed external receipts. It is for a harness interruption with preserved evidence, not for changing the source under a receipt.

The published comparison in gates/journal-report.md identifies actual run paths, quantities, disagreements and limitations. Full mutation sources and outputs remain in the private lane scratch rather than being installed as production Kernel code.


Exact structural version hashes retain generated binder labels. The collision mutation exposed conservative unrelated invalidations from those labels; the comparison report measures them. Alpha canonicalization is an explicit pending ASK in the lane REPORT, not silently treated as semantic equality.
# PE1 comparison: one Kernel slice, three observations

Run date: 2026-10-21. Checked source base: fe89edfe72f73fa17c14b28a42f81d1998337087. Kernel files and landed signatures are unchanged. PRICE PREMISES: landed theorems gaining hypotheses: none; restated: none.

