/-
# nanodregg — the one build (owner: BUILD-GATES; every layer adds its own `lean_lib`).

The file is a table, not a program: gates/tree.py reads it with a strict grammar and refuses any
top-level form it does not know (closure C0). The forms are
  * `package nanodregg where leanOptions := …` — warnings are errors, no auto-bound implicits;
  * `@[default_target] lean_lib X where globs := #[.submodules `X]` — one per layer directory,
    every file in X/ built, no umbrella module, no orphan (C1);
  * `@[default_target] lean_exe «name» where root := `M` — M holds only `main` (C7);
  * `extern_lib «ndhost»` — every Host/c/*.c, cc -Wall -Wextra -Werror, into libndhost.a. The only
    C in the tree; built from source, never a prebuilt object (ROOT ruling 2026-10-16).
No packages: Lean core and Std only (decisions/gates.md GATES-1). A bare `lake build` builds
every target, so it can never succeed by building nothing.
-/
import Lake
open Lake DSL System

package nanodregg where
  leanOptions := #[⟨`autoImplicit, false⟩, ⟨`relaxedAutoImplicit, false⟩, ⟨`warningAsError, true⟩]

-- The axiom census command (Census.Axioms): build tooling, the only place `import Lean` is
-- allowed; nothing outside Census may import it (gates/closure.py C2, C5).
@[default_target] lean_lib Census where
  globs := #[.submodules `Census]

@[default_target] lean_lib Kernel where
  globs := #[.submodules `Kernel]

@[default_target] lean_lib Protocol where
  globs := #[.submodules `Protocol]

@[default_target] lean_lib Host where
  globs := #[.submodules `Host]

@[default_target] lean_lib Lang where
  globs := #[.submodules `Lang]

@[default_target] lean_lib Codec where
  globs := #[.submodules `Codec]

@[default_target] lean_lib Hosting where
  globs := #[.submodules `Hosting]

-- LEDGER: packages over the ledger receivers (the escrow), their proofs and their journey.
@[default_target] lean_lib Ledger where
  globs := #[.submodules `Ledger]

-- HOSTING's grain lifecycle through KERNEL's receivers, with its plants (standing's sim stage).
@[default_target] lean_exe «hosting-sim» where
  root := `Hosting.Sim.Main

-- HOSTING's controller: follows one Store (Host.Tail), writes Hosting.Wire actions to grain-launch.
@[default_target] lean_exe «hosting-controller» where
  root := `Hosting.Main

-- One Lean-planned launch for launcher/tests/isolation.rs (a stand-in controller without a Store).
@[default_target] lean_exe «hosting-drive» where
  root := `Hosting.DriveMain

-- HOSTING's provider-key broker decider: keybroker's child, every ask decided by Hosting.Broker.
@[default_target] lean_exe «hosting-broker» where
  root := `Hosting.BrokerMain

-- nd-members' decider (HOSTING-33): the World's resident grains, nothing else (no clock, no key slots).
@[default_target] lean_exe «hosting-residents» where
  root := `Hosting.ResidentsMain

-- THE BAR's hosted Hermes (HOSTING-27): a resident grain's program; answers its bell through its
-- member socket with what keybroker answers on its broker socket.
@[default_target] lean_exe «resident» where
  root := `Hosting.Resident.Main


-- The Rust copy of the protocol table (client/src/generated.rs). Imports Protocol; nothing imports it.
@[default_target] lean_lib Emit where
  globs := #[.submodules `Emit]

@[default_target] lean_exe «emit-rust» where
  root := `Emit.Main

/-
# Lang.Contextual.Protocol — open protocols as typed families of continuations (lane PROTOCOL)

The object of the activities proposal's document 2: a protocol between parties is an OPEN object.
Its unspecified components are HOLES, each declared in a context `Ω` with an interface (where it
starts, what it must deliver, which reusable facts and which linear tokens it may use, which
obligations it may leave, who chooses its filling and which contract it must pass). Its
interactions with peers are `call op k` nodes whose continuation is a FAMILY indexed by the response
(`k : (r : Resp op) → Prot (next op r)`). A substitution is ONE filling per hole NAME, chosen before
anything is observed. Whether that separates a hole from an interaction depends on the NAMING, not
on the calculus: a template that puts the SAME name in every response branch gets one filling for
all of them (`Proofs.Contextual.Protocol.Coin.no_foresight`), but a template whose hole names
depend on the response (`call op fun r => hole (h r)`) gets a filling per response, which is
foresight (`response_indexed_names_have_foresight`; `foresight_iff_names_separate` is the exact
condition). Scope (one filling into every branch unchanged) is a naming discipline the author
keeps; the calculus does not enforce it. Its resources are tokens a `call` of a consuming operation
spends. The discipline is AFFINE: a token is spent at most once, and a token left unspent at `ret`
is allowed. Its executed prefix is a history (`Hist`), possibly ending in a call
whose reply was lost (`inflight`), and a re-substitution must leave every hole the history has
already entered alone (`Dispatched`).

The shape generalises minidregg's `Theory/IndexedProgram.lean` (restated in Lean core, law 11): its
`IxSignature`/`Program` gain a third constructor `hole`, its `Algebra` a hole case, its interpreter
a `stuck` outcome (doc 2 section 7: partiality visible in the result type). Nano's own free program
over effects (`Hosting.Resident.Prog`) is the instance with a trivial index and no holes
(`Proofs.Contextual.Protocol.nano_runs_iff`, `nano_interp_agrees`).

The judgment `Ω;Γ;Δ ⊢ P : Protocol(i, A) ⊣ Φ` is `HasProt sp Ω Γ Q Φ Δ P`: `Γ` the reusable facts
(hypothetical: derivability is not current availability, `admits`), `Δ` the linear tokens (a bag:
`SubBag`), `Q` the result postcondition, `Φ` the obligations any completion may still owe (an upper
bound). Substitution is SINGLE-PASS: `subst σ` replaces each hole by its filling and does not
substitute into the filling, so a filling's own holes stay open under the same `σ`. Definitions only. The statements (`HasProt`, `Runs`, `Reach`, `Started`, `Dispatched`, `SubBag`,
`Fills`, `SubstOK`, ...) are in `Lang.Proofs.Contextual.ProtocolTyping`; the theorems are in
`Lang.Proofs.Contextual.Protocol` and `Lang.Proofs.Contextual.Negotiation`.
-/

namespace Nanodregg.Lang.Contextual.Protocol

/-! ## Signatures, the accounting of an operation, polarity -/

/-- An indexed signature (mini's `IxSignature`, restated): at index `i` the operations `Op i`; each
operation's response type; the response selects the next index. -/
structure Sig (Ix : Type) where
  Op : Ix → Type
  Resp : {i : Ix} → Op i → Type
  next : {i : Ix} → (op : Op i) → Resp op → Ix

/-- What one operation does to the accounts: the linear token it SPENDS (if any), the reusable
facts it REQUIRES (authority, evidence: used, never consumed), and the obligations its DISPATCH
establishes (established when the call leaves, whatever the reply). -/
structure Spec {Ix : Type} (S : Sig Ix) (Tok Fact Ob : Type) where
  consumes : {i : Ix} → S.Op i → Option Tok
  requires : {i : Ix} → S.Op i → List Fact
  establishes : {i : Ix} → S.Op i → List Ob

/-- Who chooses a hole's filling (and, reused, which side must accept it). -/
inductive Polarity
  | ours
  | theirs
deriving DecidableEq, Repr

/-! ## Open protocols -/

/-- The free open protocol over `S` with result family `A` and hole names `Hole`: return a result,
interact (`call`: one continuation per response, at the index the response selects), or leave a
named component unspecified (`hole h`, its interface in the context `Ω`, as a CMTT metavariable
refers to the meta-context). -/
inductive Prot {Ix : Type} (S : Sig Ix) (Hole : Ix → Type) (A : Ix → Type) : Ix → Type where
  | ret {i : Ix} (a : A i) : Prot S Hole A i
  | call {i : Ix} (op : S.Op i) (k : (r : S.Resp op) → Prot S Hole A (S.next op r)) :
      Prot S Hole A i
  | hole {i : Ix} (h : Hole i) : Prot S Hole A i

section
variable {Ix : Type} {S : Sig Ix} {Hole : Ix → Type} {A : Ix → Type}

/-- A hole's interface `u :: [Γ_u; Δ_u ⊢ Protocol(i, post)] ⊣ owes`, with its polarity and an
acceptance contract that every filling must pass (`Fills`). The start index is the hole name's
index. -/
structure Iface (S : Sig Ix) (Hole : Ix → Type) (A : Ix → Type) (Tok Fact Ob : Type) (i : Ix) where
  /-- who chooses the filling -/
  pol : Polarity
  /-- the reusable facts a filling may require (`Γ_u`) -/
  ctx : List Fact
  /-- the tokens a filling may spend (`Δ_u`) -/
  need : List Tok
  /-- what every result a filling delivers satisfies -/
  post : (j : Ix) → A j → Prop
  /-- the obligations a filling may leave -/
  owes : List Ob
  /-- the acceptance contract on a filling -/
  accepts : Prot S Hole A i → Prop

/-- `Ω`: the declared interface of every unresolved component. -/
abbrev Ctx (S : Sig Ix) (Hole : Ix → Type) (A : Ix → Type) (Tok Fact Ob : Type) :=
  (i : Ix) → Hole i → Option (Iface S Hole A Tok Fact Ob i)

/-- `σ`: a partial substitution, a filling for some holes (doc 2 section 9). -/
abbrev Subst (S : Sig Ix) (Hole : Ix → Type) (A : Ix → Type) :=
  (i : Ix) → Hole i → Option (Prot S Hole A i)

/-- Typed substitution: every hole `σ` fills is replaced by its filling; nothing else moves. -/
def subst (σ : Subst S Hole A) : {i : Ix} → Prot S Hole A i → Prot S Hole A i
  | _, .ret a => .ret a
  | _, .call op k => .call op fun r => subst σ (k r)
  | i, .hole h => match σ i h with
    | some f => f
    | none => .hole h

/-- `σ` restricted to the holes `Ω` declares `ours`: a `theirs` hole is never filled. -/
def Subst.ours {Tok Fact Ob : Type} (Ω : Ctx S Hole A Tok Fact Ob) (σ : Subst S Hole A) :
    Subst S Hole A := fun i h =>
  match Ω i h with
  | some I => if I.pol = .ours then σ i h else none
  | none => none

/-- `P[σ]` under `Ω`: fill the `ours` holes `σ` names. -/
def fill {Tok Fact Ob : Type} (Ω : Ctx S Hole A Tok Fact Ob) (σ : Subst S Hole A)
    {i : Ix} (P : Prot S Hole A i) : Prot S Hole A i :=
  subst (σ.ours Ω) P

/-- The single substitution `[f/h]`. -/
def Subst.single [DecidableEq Ix] [∀ i, DecidableEq (Hole i)] {i : Ix} (h : Hole i)
    (f : Prot S Hole A i) : Subst S Hole A := fun j h' =>
  if hj : i = j then (by subst hj; exact if h' = h then some f else none) else none

/-- A signature whose response types are finite, listed. -/
structure Finite (S : Sig Ix) where
  resps : {i : Ix} → (op : S.Op i) → List (S.Resp op)
  complete : ∀ {i : Ix} (op : S.Op i) (r : S.Resp op), r ∈ resps op

/-- The holes of `P`, computed over a finite signature (`mem_holes_iff`: exactly `Occurs`). -/
def holes (fin : Finite S) : {i : Ix} → Prot S Hole A i → List (Σ j, Hole j)
  | _, .ret _ => []
  | _, .call op k => (fin.resps op).attach.flatMap fun r => holes fin (k r.1)
  | i, .hole h => [⟨i, h⟩]

/-! ## Linear tokens as a bag -/

/-! ## The judgment `Ω;Γ;Δ ⊢ P : Protocol(i, Q) ⊣ Φ` -/

/-! ## Algebras, fold, fusion -/

/-- An algebra reads an open protocol into an indexed carrier; holes too. -/
structure Algebra (S : Sig Ix) (Hole : Ix → Type) (A : Ix → Type) (C : Ix → Type) where
  ret : {i : Ix} → A i → C i
  call : {i : Ix} → (op : S.Op i) → ((r : S.Resp op) → C (S.next op r)) → C i
  hole : {i : Ix} → Hole i → C i

/-- The fold. -/
def fold {C : Ix → Type} (alg : Algebra S Hole A C) : {i : Ix} → Prot S Hole A i → C i
  | _, .ret a => alg.ret a
  | _, .call op k => alg.call op fun r => fold alg (k r)
  | _, .hole h => alg.hole h

/-- Substitution as an algebra into protocols. -/
def substAlg (σ : Subst S Hole A) : Algebra S Hole A (Prot S Hole A) where
  ret := .ret
  call := .call
  hole := fun {i} h => match σ i h with
    | some f => f
    | none => .hole h

/-- Read a template under an environment: a filled hole is read as its filling's reading, an
unfilled one as the algebra's hole. -/
def underAlg {C : Ix → Type} (alg : Algebra S Hole A C) (σ : Subst S Hole A) :
    Algebra S Hole A C where
  ret := alg.ret
  call := alg.call
  hole := fun {i} h => match σ i h with
    | some f => fold alg f
    | none => alg.hole h

/-! ## Handlers, the interpreter, partial results -/

/-- A deterministic environment: one operation against an indexed state gives a response and a
state at the index the response selects (mini's `Handler`). -/
structure Handler (S : Sig Ix) (St : Ix → Type) where
  handle : {i : Ix} → (op : S.Op i) → St i → Σ r : S.Resp op, St (S.next op r)

/-- How an interpretation ends: a result, or STUCK at an unresolved hole (never a failure). -/
inductive Result (Hole : Ix → Type) (A : Ix → Type) (St : Ix → Type) where
  | done (j : Ix) (a : A j) (s : St j)
  | stuck (j : Ix) (h : Hole j) (s : St j)

/-- The handler as a state-transformer algebra. -/
def execAlgebra {St : Ix → Type} (H : Handler S St) :
    Algebra S Hole A (fun i => St i → Result Hole A St) where
  ret := fun {i} a s => .done i a s
  call := fun op k s => match H.handle op s with
    | ⟨r, s'⟩ => k r s'
  hole := fun {i} h s => .stuck i h s

/-- Run an open protocol against an environment. -/
def interpret {St : Ix → Type} (H : Handler S St) {i : Ix} (P : Prot S Hole A i) :
    St i → Result Hole A St :=
  fold (execAlgebra H) P

/-- Run a template with its holes bound by `σ` in the environment rather than in the syntax. -/
def interpretUnder {St : Ix → Type} (H : Handler S St) (σ : Subst S Hole A) {i : Ix}
    (P : Prot S Hole A i) : St i → Result Hole A St :=
  fold (underAlg (execAlgebra H) σ) P

/-- The recording environment: `H`, and each call appended to a trace with the response it had
(the shape of nano's `recorder`). -/
def record {St : Ix → Type} (H : Handler S St) : Handler S (fun i => St i × List (Σ i, Σ op : S.Op i, S.Resp op)) where
  handle := fun {i} op p => match H.handle op p.1 with
    | ⟨r, s'⟩ => ⟨r, (s', p.2 ++ [⟨i, op, r⟩])⟩

/-! ## History -/

/-- One performed interaction: the operation, at its index, with the response it had. -/
abbrev Entry (S : Sig Ix) := Σ i, Σ op : S.Op i, S.Resp op

/-- A history of performed interactions, in order. -/
abbrev Trace (S : Sig Ix) := List (Entry S)

/-- An accepted history: the answered interactions and, possibly, ONE dispatched call whose reply
has not arrived (lost or late: `uncertain`, a state, never a license to re-plan). -/
structure Hist (S : Sig Ix) where
  answered : Trace S
  inflight : Option (Σ i, S.Op i)

/-- The tokens a trace spends. -/
def consumed {Tok Fact Ob : Type} (sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob) (t : Trace S) : List Tok :=
  t.filterMap fun e => sp.consumes e.2.1

/-- The obligations a trace established. -/
def established {Tok Fact Ob : Type} (sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob) (t : Trace S) : List Ob :=
  t.flatMap fun e => sp.establishes e.2.1

/-- The obligations a history established: the answered calls' and the in-flight call's (its
obligation stands from dispatch, whatever happened to the reply). -/
def Hist.established {Tok Fact Ob : Type} (sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob) (H : Hist S) : List Ob :=
  Protocol.established sp H.answered ++
    match H.inflight with
    | some ⟨_, op⟩ => sp.establishes op
    | none => []

/-! ## The first-class open object (doc 2 section 9) -/

/-- `(P, Ω, σ, Γ, Δ, Q, Φ, t)`: the retained TEMPLATE, its open interface, the current partial
substitution, the hypotheses and tokens, the result contract, the obligation bound, and the
accepted history. The template is kept apart from `σ`: that is what makes re-substitution possible. -/
structure Open (S : Sig Ix) (Hole : Ix → Type) (A : Ix → Type) (Tok Fact Ob : Type) (i : Ix) where
  template : Prot S Hole A i
  Ω : Ctx S Hole A Tok Fact Ob
  σ : Subst S Hole A
  Γ : List Fact
  Δ : List Tok
  Q : (j : Ix) → A j → Prop
  Φ : List Ob
  hist : Hist S

/-- The object's current protocol `P[σ]`. -/
def Open.current {Tok Fact Ob : Type} {i : Ix} (O : Open S Hole A Tok Fact Ob i) :
    Prot S Hole A i :=
  fill O.Ω O.σ O.template

/-- Replace the object's partial substitution. Data only: the GUARD (no re-substitution of a hole
the history has entered) is the statement `Open.Replan` in `Lang.Proofs.Contextual.ProtocolTyping`,
a hypothesis of every theorem about a re-plan (`Open.resubst_wf`). -/
def Open.replan {Tok Fact Ob : Type} {i : Ix} (O : Open S Hole A Tok Fact Ob i)
    (σ' : Subst S Hole A) : Open S Hole A Tok Fact Ob i :=
  { O with σ := σ' }

/-! ## Admission: current evidence, separate from derivability -/

/-- The CURRENT admission evidence: which facts hold now, which tokens are unspent now. -/
structure View (Tok Fact : Type) where
  holds : Fact → Bool
  live : Tok → Bool

/-- One concrete effect is admissible now: its facts hold and its token is unspent. -/
def admitOp {Tok Fact Ob : Type} (sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob) (v : View Tok Fact) {i : Ix}
    (op : S.Op i) : Bool :=
  (sp.requires op).all v.holds &&
    match sp.consumes op with
    | some t => v.live t
    | none => true

/-- The protocol's NEXT concrete effect is admissible now. A hole has no concrete effect to admit
(an unfinished plan describes a family of transitions; only a complete one is admitted). -/
def admits {Tok Fact Ob : Type} (sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob) (v : View Tok Fact) {i : Ix} :
    Prot S Hole A i → Bool
  | .ret _ => true
  | .call op _ => admitOp sp v op
  | .hole _ => false

/-- Durable consumption: mark a token spent. -/
def View.spend {Tok Fact : Type} [DecidableEq Tok] (v : View Tok Fact) (t : Tok) : View Tok Fact :=
  { v with live := fun t' => if t' = t then false else v.live t' }

/-- Commit one effect: refused unless admissible now; on success its token is spent durably. -/
def commit {Tok Fact Ob : Type} [DecidableEq Tok] (sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob) (v : View Tok Fact)
    {i : Ix} (op : S.Op i) : Option (View Tok Fact) :=
  if admitOp sp v op then
    some (match sp.consumes op with
      | some t => v.spend t
      | none => v)
  else none

/-- The keys an effect's admission reads: its facts and its token. -/
def opSupport {Tok Fact Ob : Type} (sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob) {i : Ix} (op : S.Op i) :
    List (Fact ⊕ Tok) :=
  (sp.requires op).map Sum.inl ++ (match sp.consumes op with
    | some t => [Sum.inr t]
    | none => [])

/-- A change of token REPRESENTATION (an authenticated representation of an unchanged semantic
token, e.g. an opening refreshed because a root moved): the spec with every token renamed. -/
def Spec.mapTok {Tok Tok' Fact Ob : Type} (e : Tok → Tok') (sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob) :
    Spec S Tok' Fact Ob where
  consumes := fun op => (sp.consumes op).map e
  requires := sp.requires
  establishes := sp.establishes

/-- An interface with its tokens renamed. -/
def Iface.mapTok {Tok Tok' Fact Ob : Type} (e : Tok → Tok') {i : Ix}
    (I : Iface S Hole A Tok Fact Ob i) : Iface S Hole A Tok' Fact Ob i :=
  { I with need := I.need.map e }

/-- A context with its tokens renamed. -/
def Ctx.mapTok {Tok Tok' Fact Ob : Type} (e : Tok → Tok') (Ω : Ctx S Hole A Tok Fact Ob) :
    Ctx S Hole A Tok' Fact Ob := fun i h => (Ω i h).map (Iface.mapTok e)

/-- A view as a store of keys. -/
def View.ofStore {Tok Fact : Type} (w : Fact ⊕ Tok → Bool) : View Tok Fact :=
  ⟨fun f => w (.inl f), fun t => w (.inr t)⟩

end

/-! ## Selective repair over fragments (doc 2 section 9, family 3) -/

/-- A checked fragment: a name, the keys its check declares it reads (its support), the check. -/
structure Frag (Name Key V : Type) where
  name : Name
  support : List Key
  check : (Key → V) → Bool

/-- Is the fragment affected by a change of `changed`? -/
def Frag.affected {Name Key V : Type} [DecidableEq Key] (f : Frag Name Key V)
    (changed : List Key) : Bool :=
  f.support.any fun k => decide (k ∈ changed)

/-- Check everything again. -/
def fromScratch {Name Key V : Type} (fs : List (Frag Name Key V)) (w : Key → V) : List Bool :=
  fs.map fun f => f.check w

/-- Selective repair: re-check the affected fragments, reuse every other cached verdict. -/
def repair {Name Key V : Type} [DecidableEq Key] :
    List (Frag Name Key V) → List Bool → List Key → (Key → V) → List Bool
  | [], _, _, _ => []
  | f :: fs, [], ch, w => f.check w :: repair fs [] ch w
  | f :: fs, c :: cs, ch, w => (if f.affected ch then f.check w else c) :: repair fs cs ch w

/-- The names of the fragments that do not check. Each name stands for one residual obligation
(re-establish that fragment); the list is `Φ′` only in that sense. -/
def residual {Name Key V : Type} : List (Frag Name Key V) → List Bool → List Name
  | [], _ => []
  | f :: fs, [] => f.name :: residual fs []
  | f :: fs, b :: bs => (if b then [] else [f.name]) ++ residual fs bs

/-- One effect's admission as a checked fragment over the store of keys. -/
def admitFrag {Ix : Type} {S : Sig Ix} {Name Tok Fact Ob : Type} (sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob)
    (name : Name) {i : Ix} (op : S.Op i) : Frag Name (Fact ⊕ Tok) Bool where
  name := name
  support := opSupport sp op
  check := fun w => admitOp sp (View.ofStore w) op

/-! ## Shared parameters: the completion space (doc 2 section 4) -/

/-- The four conditions on ONE completion `θ`. -/
structure Conds (Θ : Type) where
  typed : Θ → Prop
  guards : Θ → Prop
  authority : Θ → Prop
  resources : Θ → Prop

/-! ## Search state versus logical status (the matcher, doc 2 section 4) -/

/-- Greedy first-fit: each want in order takes the FIRST remaining offer that covers it; the count
of wants satisfied. -/
def firstFit : List Nat → List Nat → Nat
  | _, [] => 0
  | offers, w :: ws =>
    match offers.findIdx? (fun o => decide (w ≤ o)) with
    | some n => firstFit (offers.eraseIdx n) ws + 1
    | none => firstFit offers ws

/-- Complete search: is there an assignment of distinct offers covering every want? -/
def coverAll : List Nat → List Nat → Bool
  | _, [] => true
  | offers, w :: ws =>
    (List.range offers.length).any fun n =>
      decide (w ≤ offers.getD n 0) && coverAll (offers.eraseIdx n) ws

/-- A SCALAR ILLUSTRATION of shared parameters (the price alone is `θ`): the buyer accepts a price
at most 5, the seller at least 7. The same separation over `Subst` of the negotiation template is
`Proofs.Contextual.Negotiation.separate_witnesses_over_substitutions`. -/
def priceConds : Conds Nat where
  typed := fun _ => True
  guards := fun x => x ≤ 5
  authority := fun x => 7 ≤ x
  resources := fun _ => True

/-! ## Example: the committed bit (doc 2 section 5) -/

namespace Coin

/-- Before and after the peer reveals its bit. -/
inductive Phase
  | waiting
  | revealed
deriving DecidableEq, Repr

/-- The only operation: receive the peer's bit; nothing is available afterwards. -/
inductive Op : Phase → Type
  | recv : Op .waiting

def sig : Sig Phase where
  Op := Op
  Resp := fun | .recv => Bool
  next := fun | .recv, _ => .revealed

/-- One hole name, at `revealed`: our answer, planned before the reveal. -/
def HoleN : Phase → Type
  | .waiting => Empty
  | .revealed => Unit

abbrev Res : Phase → Type := fun _ => Bool

abbrev P := Prot sig HoleN Res

/-- The peer answers `b`. -/
def env (b : Bool) : Handler sig (fun _ => Unit) where
  handle := fun | .recv, () => ⟨b, ()⟩

/-- We win against `b` when the run ends with result `b`; a run stuck at a hole loses. The hole
names `Hn` are a parameter so that templates with different naming disciplines can be compared. -/
def wins {Hn : Phase → Type} {i : Phase} (b : Bool) (p : Prot sig Hn Res i) (s : Unit) : Bool :=
  match interpret (env b) p s with
  | .done _ a _ => a == b
  | .stuck _ _ _ => false

/-- The OPEN plan: receive, then do whatever our hole says. Its filling is chosen once. -/
def planHole : P .waiting := .call (S := sig) Op.recv fun _ => .hole (i := Phase.revealed) ()

/-- The RESPONSE-DEPENDENT plan: the continuation is a family over the response. -/
def planCall : P .waiting := .call (S := sig) Op.recv fun b => .ret b

/-- A template whose hole name may depend on the peer's bit: `name b` is the hole in branch `b`.
Response-free naming is the case `name true = name false`. -/
def planNamed {Hn : Phase → Type} (name : Bool → Hn .revealed) : Prot sig Hn Res .waiting :=
  .call (S := sig) Op.recv fun b => .hole (i := Phase.revealed) (name b)

/-- One hole name per possible bit at `revealed`. -/
def HoleB : Phase → Type
  | .waiting => Empty
  | .revealed => Bool

/-- The filling "answer `c`". -/
def answer (c : Bool) : Subst sig HoleN Res := fun
  | .waiting, h => nomatch h
  | .revealed, () => some (.ret c)

/-- The hole's interface, with polarity `p` (no facts, tokens or obligations in this game). -/
def iface (p : Polarity) : Iface sig HoleN Res Unit Unit Unit .revealed where
  pol := p
  ctx := []
  need := []
  post := fun _ _ => True
  owes := []
  accepts := fun _ => True

/-- `Ω` declaring the answer hole with polarity `p`. -/
def ctxOf (p : Polarity) : Ctx sig HoleN Res Unit Unit Unit := fun
  | .waiting, h => nomatch h
  | .revealed, () => some (iface p)

end Coin

/-! ## The integration experiment: a one-use capability, two providers, a deadline, a cancel
(doc 3). Definitions here; the theorems in `Lang.Proofs.Contextual.Negotiation`. -/

namespace Negotiation

/-- Two candidate providers. -/
inductive Provider
  | p1
  | p2
deriving DecidableEq, Repr

/-- Phases: idle → reserved (deposit held) → done. -/
inductive Phase
  | idle
  | reserved
  | done
deriving DecidableEq, Repr

/-- The operations. `reserve` holds the buyer's deposit; `commit p` spends the one-use capability
on provider `p` (the provider's reply: delivered or not); `cancel` abandons and refunds. -/
inductive Op : Phase → Type
  | reserve : Op .idle
  | commit (p : Provider) : Op .reserved
  | cancel : Op .reserved

def respOf : {i : Phase} → Op i → Type
  | _, .reserve => Unit
  | _, .commit _ => Bool
  | _, .cancel => Unit

def sig : Sig Phase where
  Op := Op
  Resp := respOf
  next := fun
    | .reserve, _ => .reserved
    | .commit _, _ => .done
    | .cancel, _ => .done

/-- The single linear token: the capability. -/
inductive Tok
  | cap
deriving DecidableEq, Repr

/-- Reusable facts: a provider's authority; the deadline has not passed. -/
inductive Fact
  | auth (p : Provider)
  | beforeDeadline
deriving DecidableEq, Repr

/-- Obligations: the deposit is held; pay provider `p`; refund the deposit. -/
inductive Ob
  | holdDeposit
  | pay (p : Provider)
  | refund
deriving DecidableEq, Repr

def spec : Spec sig Tok Fact Ob where
  consumes := fun
    | .commit _ => some .cap
    | _ => none
  requires := fun
    | .commit p => [.auth p, .beforeDeadline]
    | _ => []
  establishes := fun
    | .reserve => [.holdDeposit]
    | .commit p => [.pay p]
    | .cancel => [.refund]

/-- One hole: which provider, chosen by us, after the reservation. -/
def HoleN : Phase → Type
  | .reserved => Unit
  | _ => Empty

/-- Results: whether the capability's service was delivered. -/
abbrev Res : Phase → Type := fun _ => Bool

abbrev P := Prot sig HoleN Res

instance : ∀ i, DecidableEq (HoleN i)
  | .idle => fun a => nomatch a
  | .reserved => fun () () => isTrue rfl
  | .done => fun a => nomatch a

/-- The open protocol: reserve, then the provider hole. -/
def template : P .idle := .call (S := sig) Op.reserve fun _ => .hole (i := Phase.reserved) ()

/-- A candidate: commit the capability on `p`; deliver its reply. -/
def plan (p : Provider) : P .reserved := .call (S := sig) (Op.commit p) fun ok => .ret ok

/-- The cancellation path. -/
def cancelPlan : P .reserved := .call (S := sig) Op.cancel fun _ => .ret false

/-- The hole's interface: ours, accepted by us, may use both providers' authority and the
deadline, may spend the capability, may owe payment to either provider or the refund. -/
def iface : Iface sig HoleN Res Tok Fact Ob .reserved where
  pol := .ours
  ctx := [.auth .p1, .auth .p2, .beforeDeadline]
  need := [.cap]
  post := fun _ _ => True
  owes := [.pay .p1, .pay .p2, .refund]
  accepts := fun _ => True

def Ω : Ctx sig HoleN Res Tok Fact Ob := fun
  | .reserved, () => some iface
  | .idle, h => nomatch h
  | .done, h => nomatch h

/-- Choose `f` for the provider hole. -/
def choose (f : P .reserved) : Subst sig HoleN Res := fun
  | .reserved, () => some f
  | .idle, h => nomatch h
  | .done, h => nomatch h

/-- The negotiation's responses, listed. -/
def finite : Finite sig where
  resps := fun
    | .reserve => [()]
    | .commit _ => [true, false]
    | .cancel => [()]
  complete := by
    intro i op r
    cases op with
    | reserve => cases r; simp
    | commit p => cases r <;> simp
    | cancel => cases r; simp

/-- The negotiation's hypotheses, tokens and obligation bound. -/
def Γ₀ : List Fact := [.auth .p1, .auth .p2, .beforeDeadline]
def Δ₀ : List Tok := [.cap]
def Φ₀ : List Ob := [.holdDeposit, .pay .p1, .pay .p2, .refund]

/-- The open object: the template with `f` chosen for the provider hole, history `H`. -/
def obj (f : P .reserved) (H : Hist sig) : Open sig HoleN Res Tok Fact Ob .idle where
  template := template
  Ω := Ω
  σ := choose f
  Γ := Γ₀
  Δ := Δ₀
  Q := fun _ _ => True
  Φ := Φ₀
  hist := H

/-- The reservation answered. -/
def reserved : Entry sig := ⟨.idle, Op.reserve, ()⟩

/-- Reserved; nothing dispatched yet. -/
def H₀ : Hist sig := ⟨[reserved], none⟩

/-- Reserved; the commitment to `p` dispatched and its reply LOST. -/
def lost (p : Provider) : Hist sig := ⟨[reserved], some ⟨.reserved, Op.commit p⟩⟩

/-- An environment: providers deliver iff `deliver`; the state counts calls. -/
def env (deliver : Bool) : Handler sig (fun _ => Nat) where
  handle := fun op n => match op with
    | .reserve => ⟨(), n + 1⟩
    | .commit _ => ⟨deliver, n + 1⟩
    | .cancel => ⟨(), n + 1⟩

/-- The world: a clock and a deadline, provider authority, the capability's nullifier (spent or
not), and an unrelated store. -/
structure World where
  now : Nat
  deadline : Nat
  auth : Provider → Bool
  capSpent : Bool
  other : Nat → Nat

/-- What the world says to admission. -/
def World.view (w : World) : View Tok Fact where
  holds := fun
    | .auth p => w.auth p
    | .beforeDeadline => decide (w.now < w.deadline)
  live := fun .cap => !w.capSpent

/-- The candidates, numbered, in the order the plan lists them. -/
def candidates : List (Nat × P .reserved) := [(1, plan .p1), (2, plan .p2), (3, cancelPlan)]

/-- The numbers of the candidates admissible in `w` now. -/
def available (w : World) : List Nat :=
  (candidates.filter fun c => admits spec w.view c.2).map Prod.fst

/-- The world on day 0: both providers authorised, deadline 10, capability unspent. -/
def w0 : World := ⟨0, 10, fun _ => true, false, fun _ => 0⟩

/-- Revoke a provider's authority. -/
def World.revoke (w : World) (p : Provider) : World :=
  { w with auth := fun q => if q = p then false else w.auth q }

/-- A commitment against the world: refused unless admissible, then the nullifier is spent. -/
def World.commit (w : World) {i : Phase} (op : Op i) : Option World :=
  if admitOp spec w.view (S := sig) op then
    some (match spec.consumes (S := sig) op with
      | some .cap => { w with capSpent := true }
      | none => w)
  else none

/-- The candidate fragments for selective repair: each candidate's admission, over the keys of
its first effect. -/
def frags : List (Frag Nat (Fact ⊕ Tok) Bool) :=
  [admitFrag spec 1 (S := sig) (Op.commit .p1), admitFrag spec 2 (S := sig) (Op.commit .p2),
    admitFrag spec 3 (S := sig) Op.cancel]

/-- A second representation of the capability token: its opening under the root of an epoch.
Openings from different epochs are different representations of the same capability. -/
inductive Tok'
  | capAt (epoch : Nat)
deriving DecidableEq, Repr

/-- The representation under epoch `E`. -/
def Tok.at (E : Nat) : Tok → Tok'
  | .cap => .capAt E

/-- The PARTIAL correspondence back: only an opening from the current epoch `E` names the token. -/
def Tok'.current (E : Nat) : Tok' → Option Tok
  | .capAt e => if e = E then some .cap else none

/-- The world's admission view over the new representation at current epoch `E`: an opening is
live only when it is from epoch `E` and the token it names is unspent. A stale opening is not. -/
def World.viewAt (w : World) (E : Nat) : View Tok' Fact where
  holds := w.view.holds
  live := fun t => match t.current E with
    | some t₀ => w.view.live t₀
    | none => false

/-- The world as a store of keys. -/
def World.store (w : World) : Fact ⊕ Tok → Bool
  | .inl f => w.view.holds f
  | .inr t => w.view.live t

/-! ### Internal once versus external once -/

/-- The external side of one commitment: how many times the network delivered the dispatched
request, whether the provider deduplicates by the request identity, and so how many times the
service was performed. -/
structure External where
  deliveries : Nat
  dedupe : Bool

def External.executions (e : External) : Nat :=
  if e.dedupe then min e.deliveries 1 else e.deliveries

/-- What the internal model records about one commitment: the nullifier spent and the reply
(`none`: lost). -/
structure Internal where
  capSpent : Bool
  reply : Option Bool

/-- The reply an answered entry carries, if it is a commitment. -/
def entryReply : Entry sig → Option Bool
  | ⟨_, op, r⟩ => match op, r with
    | .commit _, b => some b
    | .reserve, _ => none
    | .cancel, _ => none

/-- Is an in-flight call a commitment? -/
def inflightSpends : Option (Σ i, sig.Op i) → Bool
  | some ⟨_, .commit _⟩ => true
  | _ => false

/-- The internal record, READ OFF a history: the nullifier is spent when an answered or in-flight
call spent the capability; the reply is the answered commitment's. -/
def Internal.ofHist (H : Hist sig) : Internal where
  capSpent := (consumed spec H.answered).contains .cap || inflightSpends H.inflight
  reply := H.answered.findSome? entryReply

/-- Reserved, then the commitment to `p` answered with `b`. -/
def answeredH (p : Provider) (b : Bool) : Hist sig :=
  ⟨[reserved, ⟨.reserved, Op.commit p, b⟩], none⟩

/-- A filling with the same first call as `plan p` but a different continuation. -/
def planFlip (p : Provider) : P .reserved := .call (S := sig) (Op.commit p) fun ok => .ret (!ok)

end Negotiation

end Nanodregg.Lang.Contextual.Protocol
/-
# Lang.Proofs.Contextual.Protocol — the theory of open protocols (lane PROTOCOL)

The four theorem families of the proposal's document 2 section 9, over `Lang.Contextual.Protocol`:

* CONTEXTUAL COMPLETION: `fill_preserves_hasProt` (a filling satisfying the hole's interface:
  index, context, tokens, result, obligations, polarity, acceptance; preserves the judgment);
  `fill_skips_theirs`, `theirs_hole_untypable` (DESIGN RULES, stated as theorems so they are
  checked: `fill` restricts to `ours` holes by definition and the hole rule requires `ours`).
* INTERPRETATION OF SUBSTITUTION: `fold_fusion`, `fold_subst`, `interpret_fill` (interpreting
  `P[σ]` IS interpreting the template with `σ` in the environment), via fusion.
* SELECTIVE REPAIR: `locality`, `repair_agrees_from_scratch`, `repair_residual`, `repair_reuses`.
* ADMISSION AND HISTORY PRESERVATION: `hasProt_reach` (subject reduction: the AFFINE token account
  and the obligations of every prefix; `at_most_once`), `resubst_preserves_started` /
  `Open.resubst_wf` (re-substituting an unentered hole preserves the accepted history and its
  obligations), `admits_local`, `commit_once`; the teeth for the guard are in the negotiation
  (`Negotiation.lost_reply_blocks_replan`, `answered_blocks_replan`, `guard_stricter_than_wf`).

And document 2 sections 4 and 5: `Coin.foresight_iff_names_separate` (a hole separates from an
interaction exactly when its NAME does not depend on the response: a naming discipline, not a fact
of the calculus), `Coin.no_foresight`, `Coin.response_indexed_names_have_foresight`,
`Coin.response_dependent_succeeds`; the scalar illustrations `separate_witnesses_insufficient`,
`greedy_vs_logical` (the substitution-level form is `Negotiation.separate_witnesses_over_substitutions`). The relation to nano's own
free program over effects: `nano_runs_iff`, `nano_interp_agrees`, `nano_interp_runs`.
-/
import Lang.Proofs.Contextual.ProtocolTyping
import Lang.Contextual.NanoBridge
import Hosting.Proofs.ResidentRun

namespace Nanodregg.Lang.Contextual.Protocol

section
variable {Ix : Type} {S : Sig Ix} {Hole : Ix → Type} {A : Ix → Type}
variable {Tok Fact Ob : Type}

/-! ## Bags -/

theorem SubBag.refl [DecidableEq Tok] (Δ : List Tok) : SubBag Δ Δ := fun _ => Nat.le_refl _

theorem SubBag.trans [DecidableEq Tok] {Δ₁ Δ₂ Δ₃ : List Tok} (h₁ : SubBag Δ₁ Δ₂)
    (h₂ : SubBag Δ₂ Δ₃) : SubBag Δ₁ Δ₃ := fun t => Nat.le_trans (h₁ t) (h₂ t)

theorem SubBag.mem [DecidableEq Tok] {Δ₁ Δ₂ : List Tok} (h : SubBag Δ₁ Δ₂) {t : Tok}
    (ht : t ∈ Δ₁) : t ∈ Δ₂ :=
  List.count_pos_iff.mp (Nat.lt_of_lt_of_le (List.count_pos_iff.mpr ht) (h t))

theorem SubBag.erase [DecidableEq Tok] {Δ₁ Δ₂ : List Tok} (h : SubBag Δ₁ Δ₂) (t : Tok) :
    SubBag (Δ₁.erase t) (Δ₂.erase t) := by
  intro a
  rw [List.count_erase, List.count_erase]
  exact Nat.sub_le_sub_right (h a) _

/-! ## Contextual completion -/

/-- Weakening: more facts, a weaker postcondition, more permitted obligations, more tokens. -/
theorem HasProt.weaken [DecidableEq Tok] {sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob}
    {Ω : Ctx S Hole A Tok Fact Ob} {Γ Γ' : List Fact} {Q Q' : (j : Ix) → A j → Prop}
    {Φ Φ' : List Ob} (hΓ : ∀ f ∈ Γ, f ∈ Γ') (hQ : ∀ j a, Q j a → Q' j a)
    (hΦ : ∀ o ∈ Φ, o ∈ Φ') {Δ Δ' : List Tok} {i : Ix} {P : Prot S Hole A i}
    (h : HasProt sp Ω Γ Q Φ Δ P) (hΔ : SubBag Δ Δ') : HasProt sp Ω Γ' Q' Φ' Δ' P := by
  induction h generalizing Δ' with
  | ret a hq => exact .ret a (hQ _ _ hq)
  | call op k hc hr he _ ih =>
    exact .call op k hc (fun f hf => hΓ f (hr f hf)) (fun o ho => hΦ o (he o ho))
      (fun r => ih r hΔ)
  | spend op k t hc ht hr he _ ih =>
    exact .spend op k t hc (hΔ.mem ht) (fun f hf => hΓ f (hr f hf)) (fun o ho => hΦ o (he o ho))
      (fun r => ih r (hΔ.erase t))
  | hole h I hI hp hctx hneed hpost howes =>
    exact .hole h I hI hp (fun f hf => hΓ f (hctx f hf)) (hneed.trans hΔ)
      (fun j a ha => hQ j a (hpost j a ha)) (fun o ho => hΦ o (howes o ho))

/-- Substituting an interface-respecting substitution preserves the judgment. -/
theorem subst_preserves_hasProt [DecidableEq Tok] {sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob}
    {Ω : Ctx S Hole A Tok Fact Ob} {σ : Subst S Hole A} (hσ : SubstOK sp Ω σ)
    {Γ : List Fact} {Q : (j : Ix) → A j → Prop} {Φ : List Ob} {Δ : List Tok} {i : Ix}
    {P : Prot S Hole A i} (h : HasProt sp Ω Γ Q Φ Δ P) : HasProt sp Ω Γ Q Φ Δ (subst σ P) := by
  induction h with
  | ret a hq => exact .ret a hq
  | call op k hc hr he _ ih => exact .call op _ hc hr he ih
  | spend op k t hc ht hr he _ ih => exact .spend op _ t hc ht hr he ih
  | @hole Δ i h I hI hp hctx hneed hpost howes =>
    show HasProt sp Ω Γ Q Φ Δ (match σ i h with | some f => f | none => .hole h)
    cases hs : σ i h with
    | none => exact .hole h I hI hp hctx hneed hpost howes
    | some f =>
      obtain ⟨I', hI', _, hf, _⟩ := hσ i h f hs
      rw [hI] at hI'
      cases hI'
      exact hf.weaken hctx hpost howes hneed

/-- Restricting to `ours` keeps a substitution interface-respecting. -/
theorem SubstOK.ours [DecidableEq Tok] {sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob} {Ω : Ctx S Hole A Tok Fact Ob}
    {σ : Subst S Hole A} (hσ : SubstOK sp Ω σ) : SubstOK sp Ω (σ.ours Ω) := by
  intro i h f hs
  unfold Subst.ours at hs
  split at hs
  · split at hs
    · exact hσ i h f hs
    · cases hs
  · cases hs

/-- **Contextual completion** (family 1): filling the holes of a judged protocol with fillings that
satisfy their interfaces preserves the protocol's judgment, at the same facts, tokens, result
contract and obligation bound. -/
theorem fill_preserves_hasProt [DecidableEq Tok] {sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob}
    {Ω : Ctx S Hole A Tok Fact Ob} {σ : Subst S Hole A} (hσ : SubstOK sp Ω σ)
    {Γ : List Fact} {Q : (j : Ix) → A j → Prop} {Φ : List Ob} {Δ : List Tok} {i : Ix}
    {P : Prot S Hole A i} (h : HasProt sp Ω Γ Q Φ Δ P) :
    HasProt sp Ω Γ Q Φ Δ (fill Ω σ P) :=
  subst_preserves_hasProt hσ.ours h

/-- **Polarity, a design rule**: `fill` never fills a hole `Ω` declares `theirs`, whatever `σ`
offers. True by the definition of `Subst.ours`; stated so the rule is checked, not as a finding. -/
theorem fill_skips_theirs {Ω : Ctx S Hole A Tok Fact Ob} (σ : Subst S Hole A) {i : Ix}
    {h : Hole i} {I : Iface S Hole A Tok Fact Ob i} (hI : Ω i h = some I)
    (hp : I.pol = .theirs) : fill Ω σ (.hole h) = .hole h := by
  simp [fill, subst, Subst.ours, hI, hp]

/-- **Polarity, a design rule**: a `theirs` hole is not a judged protocol, because the `hole` rule of
`HasProt` requires `ours`. Another participant's choice must be written as a `call` whose response
selects the continuation. Stated so the rule is checked, not as a finding. -/
theorem theirs_hole_untypable [DecidableEq Tok] {sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob}
    {Ω : Ctx S Hole A Tok Fact Ob} {Γ : List Fact} {Q : (j : Ix) → A j → Prop} {Φ : List Ob}
    {Δ : List Tok} {i : Ix} {h : Hole i} {I : Iface S Hole A Tok Fact Ob i}
    (hI : Ω i h = some I) (hp : I.pol = .theirs) : ¬ HasProt sp Ω Γ Q Φ Δ (.hole h) := by
  intro hh
  cases hh with
  | hole _ I' hI' hp' =>
    rw [hI] at hI'
    cases hI'
    rw [hp] at hp'
    cases hp'

/-- On interface-respecting substitutions `fill` is plain substitution. -/
theorem fill_eq_subst [DecidableEq Tok] {sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob} {Ω : Ctx S Hole A Tok Fact Ob}
    {σ : Subst S Hole A} (hσ : SubstOK sp Ω σ) {i : Ix} (P : Prot S Hole A i) :
    fill Ω σ P = subst σ P := by
  have : σ.ours Ω = σ := by
    funext j h
    unfold Subst.ours
    cases hs : σ j h with
    | none => split <;> (try split) <;> rfl
    | some f =>
      obtain ⟨I, hI, hp, _⟩ := hσ j h f hs
      simp [hI, hp]
  simp [fill, this]

/-! ## Holes -/

/-- `holes` computes exactly the holes that occur. -/
theorem mem_holes_iff (fin : Finite S) {i : Ix} (P : Prot S Hole A i) (j : Ix) (h : Hole j) :
    (⟨j, h⟩ : Σ j, Hole j) ∈ holes fin P ↔ Occurs P j h := by
  induction P with
  | ret a =>
    simp only [holes, List.not_mem_nil, false_iff]
    intro ho; cases ho
  | call op k ih =>
    simp only [holes, List.mem_flatMap, List.mem_attach, true_and]
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨⟨r, _⟩, hm⟩
      exact .call r ((ih r).mp hm)
    · intro ho
      cases ho with
      | call r ho => exact ⟨⟨r, fin.complete op r⟩, (ih r).mpr ho⟩
  | @hole i h' =>
    simp only [holes, List.mem_singleton]
    constructor
    · intro he
      cases he
      exact .here h
    · intro ho
      cases ho
      rfl

/-- A substitution that fills no occurring hole leaves the protocol alone. -/
theorem subst_away {σ : Subst S Hole A} {i : Ix} (P : Prot S Hole A i)
    (hσ : ∀ j h, Occurs P j h → σ j h = none) : subst σ P = P := by
  induction P with
  | ret a => rfl
  | call op k ih =>
    show Prot.call op (fun r => subst σ (k r)) = _
    congr 1
    funext r
    exact ih r fun j h ho => hσ j h (.call r ho)
  | @hole i h =>
    show (match σ i h with | some f => f | none => .hole h) = _
    rw [hσ i h (.here h)]

/-! ## Interpretation of substitution -/

/-- **Fold fusion**: an algebra morphism commutes with the fold (the carriers may differ). -/
theorem fold_fusion {C D : Ix → Type} {src : Algebra S Hole A C} {dst : Algebra S Hole A D}
    {φ : (i : Ix) → C i → D i} (hφ : AlgebraHom src dst φ) {i : Ix} (P : Prot S Hole A i) :
    φ i (fold src P) = fold dst P := by
  induction P with
  | ret a => exact hφ.ret a
  | call op k ih =>
    show φ _ (src.call op fun r => fold src (k r)) = dst.call op fun r => fold dst (k r)
    rw [hφ.call]
    congr 1
    funext r
    exact ih r
  | hole h => exact hφ.hole h

/-- Substitution is the fold of the substitution algebra. -/
theorem subst_eq_fold (σ : Subst S Hole A) {i : Ix} (P : Prot S Hole A i) :
    subst σ P = fold (substAlg σ) P := by
  induction P with
  | ret a => rfl
  | call op k ih =>
    show Prot.call op (fun r => subst σ (k r)) = Prot.call op (fun r => fold (substAlg σ) (k r))
    congr 1
    funext r
    exact ih r
  | hole h => rfl

/-- Reading a substituted protocol is a morphism from the substitution algebra to the template's
reading under the environment. -/
theorem underHom {C : Ix → Type} (alg : Algebra S Hole A C) (σ : Subst S Hole A) :
    AlgebraHom (substAlg σ) (underAlg alg σ) (fun _ P => fold alg P) where
  ret := fun _ => rfl
  call := fun _ _ => rfl
  hole := fun {i} h => by
    show fold alg (match σ i h with | some f => f | none => .hole h) =
      (match σ i h with | some f => fold alg f | none => alg.hole h)
    cases σ i h <;> rfl

/-- **The substitution lemma for readings**: reading `P[σ]` is reading the template `P` with
`σ` bound in the environment. Proved by fusion. -/
theorem fold_subst {C : Ix → Type} (alg : Algebra S Hole A C) (σ : Subst S Hole A) {i : Ix}
    (P : Prot S Hole A i) : fold alg (subst σ P) = fold (underAlg alg σ) P := by
  rw [subst_eq_fold]
  exact fold_fusion (underHom alg σ) P

/-- **Interpretation of substitution** (family 2): running the instantiated protocol against an
environment is running its template with the substitution in the environment. -/
theorem interpret_fill {St : Ix → Type} (H : Handler S St) (σ : Subst S Hole A) {i : Ix}
    (P : Prot S Hole A i) : interpret H (subst σ P) = interpretUnder H σ P :=
  fold_subst (execAlgebra H) σ P

/-! ## Paths and prefixes -/

theorem runs_reach {i : Ix} {P : Prot S Hole A i} {t : Trace S} {j : Ix} {a : A j}
    (h : Runs P t j a) : Reach P t ⟨j, .ret a⟩ := by
  induction h with
  | ret a => exact .here _
  | call r _ ih => exact .call r ih

theorem reach_append {i : Ix} {P : Prot S Hole A i} {t₁ t₂ : Trace S}
    {R₀ R : Σ j, Prot S Hole A j} (h₁ : Reach P t₁ R₀) (h₂ : Reach R₀.2 t₂ R) :
    Reach P (t₁ ++ t₂) R := by
  induction h₁ with
  | here => exact h₂
  | call r _ ih => exact .call r (ih h₂)

/-- A prefix of the template is a prefix of every instance, leaving the instance's residual. -/
theorem reach_subst (σ : Subst S Hole A) {i : Ix} {P : Prot S Hole A i} {t : Trace S}
    {R : Σ j, Prot S Hole A j} (h : Reach P t R) : Reach (subst σ P) t ⟨R.1, subst σ R.2⟩ := by
  induction h with
  | here => exact .here _
  | call r _ ih => exact .call r ih

/-- A path that enters a filled hole: the template's prefix to the hole, then the filling's. -/
theorem reach_through_hole {σ : Subst S Hole A} {i : Ix} {P : Prot S Hole A i} {t₁ t₂ : Trace S}
    {j : Ix} {h : Hole j} {f : Prot S Hole A j} {R : Σ j, Prot S Hole A j}
    (h₁ : Reach P t₁ ⟨j, .hole h⟩) (hs : σ j h = some f) (h₂ : Reach f t₂ R) :
    Reach (subst σ P) (t₁ ++ t₂) R := by
  have := reach_subst σ h₁
  have e : subst σ (Prot.hole (S := S) (A := A) h) = f := by simp [subst, hs]
  exact reach_append this (by simpa [e] using h₂)

/-- Every prefix of an instance either stays in the template or enters a filled hole and goes on. -/
theorem reach_subst_cases {σ : Subst S Hole A} {i : Ix} {P : Prot S Hole A i} {t : Trace S}
    {R : Σ j, Prot S Hole A j} (hr : Reach (subst σ P) t R) :
    (∃ R₀ : Σ j, Prot S Hole A j, Reach P t R₀ ∧ R = ⟨R₀.1, subst σ R₀.2⟩) ∨
    (∃ t₁ t₂ j, ∃ h : Hole j, ∃ f, t = t₁ ++ t₂ ∧ t₂ ≠ [] ∧ Reach P t₁ ⟨j, .hole h⟩ ∧
      σ j h = some f ∧ Reach f t₂ R) := by
  induction P generalizing t with
  | ret a =>
    cases hr
    exact .inl ⟨_, .here _, rfl⟩
  | call op k ih =>
    cases hr with
    | here => exact .inl ⟨_, .here _, rfl⟩
    | call r hr =>
      rcases ih r hr with ⟨R₀, h0, e⟩ | ⟨t₁, t₂, j, h, f, ht, hne, h1, hs, h2⟩
      · exact .inl ⟨R₀, .call r h0, e⟩
      · exact .inr ⟨_ :: t₁, t₂, j, h, f, by simp [ht], hne, .call r h1, hs, h2⟩
  | @hole i h =>
    change Reach (match σ i h with | some f => f | none => .hole h) t R at hr
    cases hs : σ i h with
    | none =>
      rw [hs] at hr
      cases hr
      exact .inl ⟨_, .here _, by simp [subst, hs]⟩
    | some f =>
      rw [hs] at hr
      cases t with
      | nil =>
        cases hr
        exact .inl ⟨_, .here _, by simp [subst, hs]⟩
      | cons e t => exact .inr ⟨[], e :: t, i, h, f, rfl, by simp, .here _, hs, hr⟩

/-! ## Subject reduction: the linear account and the obligations of a prefix -/

theorem consumed_cons (sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob) (e : Entry S) (t : Trace S) :
    consumed sp (e :: t) = (match sp.consumes e.2.1 with | some x => [x] | none => []) ++
      consumed sp t := by
  simp only [consumed, List.filterMap_cons]
  cases sp.consumes e.2.1 <;> rfl

/-- **Subject reduction along a prefix**: every prefix of a judged protocol spends tokens within
`Δ` (as a bag: each token at most as often as `Δ` holds it, together with what the residual still
holds), establishes only obligations within `Φ`, and leaves a residual judged at the remaining
tokens. -/
theorem hasProt_reach [DecidableEq Tok] {sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob} {Ω : Ctx S Hole A Tok Fact Ob}
    {Γ : List Fact} {Q : (j : Ix) → A j → Prop} {Φ : List Ob} {Δ : List Tok} {i : Ix}
    {P : Prot S Hole A i} {t : Trace S} {R : Σ j, Prot S Hole A j}
    (h : HasProt sp Ω Γ Q Φ Δ P) (hr : Reach P t R) :
    ∃ Δ', HasProt sp Ω Γ Q Φ Δ' R.2 ∧
      (∀ x, (consumed sp t).count x + Δ'.count x ≤ Δ.count x) ∧
      ∀ o ∈ established sp t, o ∈ Φ := by
  induction hr generalizing Δ with
  | here => exact ⟨Δ, h, by simp [consumed], by simp [established]⟩
  | @call i op k tr R r _ ih =>
    cases h with
    | call _ _ hc _ he hk =>
      obtain ⟨Δ', h', hcount, hob⟩ := ih (hk r)
      refine ⟨Δ', h', ?_, ?_⟩
      · intro x
        rw [consumed_cons]
        simp only [hc, List.nil_append]
        exact hcount x
      · intro o ho
        simp only [established, List.flatMap_cons, List.mem_append] at ho
        rcases ho with ho | ho
        · exact he o ho
        · exact hob o ho
    | spend _ _ t₀ hc ht _ he hk =>
      obtain ⟨Δ', h', hcount, hob⟩ := ih (hk r)
      refine ⟨Δ', h', ?_, ?_⟩
      · intro x
        rw [consumed_cons]
        simp only [hc, List.singleton_append, List.count_cons]
        have hx := hcount x
        rw [List.count_erase] at hx
        have hpos : 0 < Δ.count t₀ := List.count_pos_iff.mpr ht
        by_cases hxt : t₀ = x
        · subst hxt
          simp at hx ⊢
          omega
        · have : (t₀ == x) = false := by simpa using hxt
          simp [this] at hx ⊢
          omega
      · intro o ho
        simp only [established, List.flatMap_cons, List.mem_append] at ho
        rcases ho with ho | ho
        · exact he o ho
        · exact hob o ho

/-- **At most once** (the discipline is AFFINE: `ret` accepts any leftover `Δ`, so a token may also
go unspent): a token `Δ` holds once is spent at most once on any path of a judged protocol. -/
theorem at_most_once [DecidableEq Tok] {sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob} {Ω : Ctx S Hole A Tok Fact Ob}
    {Γ : List Fact} {Q : (j : Ix) → A j → Prop} {Φ : List Ob} {Δ : List Tok} {i : Ix}
    {P : Prot S Hole A i} {t : Trace S} {R : Σ j, Prot S Hole A j} {x : Tok}
    (h : HasProt sp Ω Γ Q Φ Δ P) (hr : Reach P t R) (hx : Δ.count x ≤ 1) :
    (consumed sp t).count x ≤ 1 := by
  obtain ⟨Δ', _, hc, _⟩ := hasProt_reach h hr
  have := hc x
  omega

/-- A complete path of a judged protocol ends in a result within `Q`. -/
theorem hasProt_runs [DecidableEq Tok] {sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob} {Ω : Ctx S Hole A Tok Fact Ob}
    {Γ : List Fact} {Q : (j : Ix) → A j → Prop} {Φ : List Ob} {Δ : List Tok} {i : Ix}
    {P : Prot S Hole A i} {t : Trace S} {j : Ix} {a : A j}
    (h : HasProt sp Ω Γ Q Φ Δ P) (hr : Runs P t j a) : Q j a := by
  obtain ⟨Δ', h', _, _⟩ := hasProt_reach h (runs_reach hr)
  cases h' with
  | ret _ hq => exact hq

/-! ## History preservation under re-substitution -/

/-- The residual is a call of `o`. -/
def IsCall : (Σ j, Prot S Hole A j) → (Σ j, S.Op j) → Prop
  | ⟨j, .call op _⟩, o => o = ⟨j, op⟩
  | _, _ => False

theorem started_some_iff {i : Ix} {P : Prot S Hole A i} {t : Trace S} {o : Σ j, S.Op j} :
    Started P ⟨t, some o⟩ ↔ ∃ R, Reach P t R ∧ IsCall R o := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    cases h with
    | uncertain hr => exact ⟨_, hr, rfl⟩
  · rintro ⟨⟨j, R⟩, hr, hc⟩
    cases R with
    | ret => exact hc.elim
    | hole => exact hc.elim
    | call op k =>
      cases hc
      exact .uncertain hr

/-- **History preservation** (doc 2 section 8): replacing the filling of every hole the history has
NOT entered preserves the accepted history, answered calls and the in-flight call alike. -/
theorem resubst_preserves_started {σ σ' : Subst S Hole A} {i : Ix} {P : Prot S Hole A i}
    {H : Hist S} (hs : Started (subst σ P) H)
    (hg : ∀ j h, Dispatched P H j h → σ' j h = σ j h) : Started (subst σ' P) H := by
  obtain ⟨t, o⟩ := H
  cases o with
  | none =>
    cases hs with
    | settled hr =>
      rcases reach_subst_cases hr with ⟨R₀, h0, _⟩ | ⟨t₁, t₂, j, h, f, ht, hne, h1, hsf, h2⟩
      · exact .settled (reach_subst σ' h0)
      · have hd : Dispatched P ⟨t, none⟩ j h := ⟨t₁, t₂, ht, h1, .inl hne⟩
        rw [ht]
        exact .settled (reach_through_hole h1 ((hg j h hd).trans hsf) h2)
  | some o =>
    obtain ⟨R, hr, hc⟩ := started_some_iff.mp hs
    apply started_some_iff.mpr
    rcases reach_subst_cases hr with ⟨⟨j, R₀⟩, h0, e⟩ | ⟨t₁, t₂, j, h, f, ht, hne, h1, hsf, h2⟩
    · subst e
      cases R₀ with
      | ret a => exact hc.elim
      | call op k => exact ⟨_, reach_subst σ' h0, hc⟩
      | hole h =>
        have hd : Dispatched P ⟨t, some o⟩ j h := ⟨t, [], by simp, h0, .inr rfl⟩
        refine ⟨_, reach_subst σ' h0, ?_⟩
        have e : subst σ' (Prot.hole (S := S) (A := A) h) = subst σ (Prot.hole h) := by
          simp [subst, hg j h hd]
        simpa [e] using hc
    · have hd : Dispatched P ⟨t, some o⟩ j h := ⟨t₁, t₂, ht, h1, .inl hne⟩
      rw [show t = t₁ ++ t₂ from ht]
      exact ⟨R, reach_through_hole h1 ((hg j h hd).trans hsf) h2, hc⟩

/-- The obligations a history of a judged protocol established, the in-flight call's included,
are within `Φ`. -/
theorem started_obligations [DecidableEq Tok] {sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob}
    {Ω : Ctx S Hole A Tok Fact Ob} {Γ : List Fact} {Q : (j : Ix) → A j → Prop} {Φ : List Ob}
    {Δ : List Tok} {i : Ix} {P : Prot S Hole A i} {H : Hist S}
    (h : HasProt sp Ω Γ Q Φ Δ P) (hs : Started P H) : ∀ o ∈ H.established sp, o ∈ Φ := by
  cases hs with
  | settled hr =>
    obtain ⟨_, _, _, hob⟩ := hasProt_reach h hr
    simpa [Hist.established] using hob
  | uncertain hr =>
    obtain ⟨_, h', _, hob⟩ := hasProt_reach h hr
    intro o ho
    simp only [Hist.established, List.mem_append] at ho
    rcases ho with ho | ho
    · exact hob o ho
    · cases h' with
      | call _ _ _ _ he _ => exact he o ho
      | spend _ _ _ _ _ _ he _ => exact he o ho

/-- **Admission and history preservation for the open object**: a guarded re-substitution of a
well-formed object by an interface-respecting substitution is well-formed, keeps the accepted
history (answered and in flight), and every obligation that history established stays within the
object's bound. -/
theorem Open.resubst_wf [DecidableEq Tok] {sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob} {i : Ix}
    {O : Open S Hole A Tok Fact Ob i} (hO : O.WF sp) {σ' : Subst S Hole A}
    (hσ' : SubstOK sp O.Ω σ')
    (g : O.Replan σ') :
    (O.replan σ').WF sp ∧ (O.replan σ').hist = O.hist ∧
      ∀ o ∈ (O.replan σ').hist.established sp, o ∈ O.Φ := by
  have hst : Started (O.replan σ').current O.hist :=
    resubst_preserves_started (σ := O.σ.ours O.Ω) hO.started g
  have hwf : (O.replan σ').WF sp := ⟨hO.typed, hσ', hst⟩
  exact ⟨hwf, rfl, started_obligations (fill_preserves_hasProt hσ' hO.typed) hst⟩

/-! ## The recording interpreter performs exactly a path -/

/-- **`interpret` performs exactly a path** (nano's `interp_runs`, for open protocols): at the
recording environment, a run that ends appends to the trace exactly a complete path ending in its
result; a run that stops at a hole appends exactly a prefix reaching that hole. -/
theorem interpret_record {St : Ix → Type} (H : Handler S St) {i : Ix} (P : Prot S Hole A i)
    (s : St i) (tr₀ : Trace S) :
    match interpret (record H) P (s, tr₀) with
    | .done j a p => ∃ tr, p.2 = tr₀ ++ tr ∧ Runs P tr j a
    | .stuck j h p => ∃ tr, p.2 = tr₀ ++ tr ∧ Reach P tr ⟨j, .hole h⟩ := by
  obtain ⟨handle⟩ := H
  induction P generalizing tr₀ with
  | ret a => exact ⟨[], by simp, .ret a⟩
  | @call i op k ih =>
    rcases hh : handle op s with ⟨r, s'⟩
    have e : interpret (record ⟨handle⟩) (Prot.call op k) (s, tr₀) =
        interpret (record ⟨handle⟩) (k r) (s', tr₀ ++ [⟨i, op, r⟩]) := by
      simp only [interpret, fold, execAlgebra, record]
      rw [hh]
    rw [e]
    have := ih r s' (tr₀ ++ [⟨i, op, r⟩])
    revert this
    cases interpret (record ⟨handle⟩) (k r) (s', tr₀ ++ [⟨i, op, r⟩]) with
    | done j a p =>
      rintro ⟨tr, htr, hrun⟩
      exact ⟨_ :: tr, by simp [htr], .call r hrun⟩
    | stuck j h p =>
      rintro ⟨tr, htr, hrun⟩
      exact ⟨_ :: tr, by simp [htr], .call r hrun⟩
  | hole h => exact ⟨[], by simp, .here _⟩

/-! ## Admission: current evidence -/

theorem all_congr' {α : Type} {g g' : α → Bool} :
    ∀ l : List α, (∀ x ∈ l, g x = g' x) → l.all g = l.all g'
  | [], _ => rfl
  | x :: l, h => by
    simp only [List.all_cons]
    rw [h x (by simp), all_congr' l (fun y hy => h y (by simp [hy]))]

/-- **Locality of admission**: an effect's admission reads only its support. -/
theorem admits_local {sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob} {i : Ix} (op : S.Op i)
    {w₁ w₂ : Fact ⊕ Tok → Bool} (hw : ∀ k ∈ opSupport sp op, w₁ k = w₂ k) :
    admitOp sp (View.ofStore w₁) op = admitOp sp (View.ofStore w₂) op := by
  unfold admitOp View.ofStore
  rw [all_congr' (sp.requires op) (fun f hf => hw (.inl f) (by simp [opSupport, hf]))]
  congr 1
  cases hc : sp.consumes op with
  | none => rfl
  | some t => exact hw (.inr t) (by simp [opSupport, hc])

/-- An admission fragment declares a sufficient support. -/
theorem admitFrag_readsOnly {Name : Type} (sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob) (name : Name) {i : Ix}
    (op : S.Op i) : (admitFrag sp name op).ReadsOnly :=
  fun _ _ hw => admits_local op hw

/-- What an admitted call establishes: its facts hold now, its token is unspent now. -/
theorem admitOp_sound {sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob} {v : View Tok Fact} {i : Ix} {op : S.Op i}
    (h : admitOp sp v op = true) :
    (∀ f ∈ sp.requires op, v.holds f = true) ∧ ∀ t, sp.consumes op = some t → v.live t = true := by
  unfold admitOp at h
  simp only [Bool.and_eq_true, List.all_eq_true] at h
  refine ⟨h.1, fun t ht => ?_⟩
  have := h.2
  rw [ht] at this
  exact this

/-- **Durable consumption**: once an effect spending `t` commits, no effect spending `t` commits
again from the resulting view: a replayed or competing commitment is refused. -/
theorem commit_once [DecidableEq Tok] {sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob} {v v' : View Tok Fact} {i : Ix}
    {op : S.Op i} {t : Tok} (h : commit sp v op = some v') (ht : sp.consumes op = some t)
    {j : Ix} (op' : S.Op j) (ht' : sp.consumes op' = some t) : commit sp v' op' = none := by
  unfold commit at h
  split at h
  · simp only [ht, Option.some.injEq] at h
    subst h
    unfold commit admitOp
    simp [ht', View.spend]
  · cases h

/-! ## Selective repair -/

theorem Frag.unaffected {Name Key V : Type} [DecidableEq Key] {f : Frag Name Key V}
    {changed : List Key} (h : f.affected changed = false) : ∀ k ∈ f.support, k ∉ changed := by
  intro k hk hc
  have : f.affected changed = true := List.any_eq_true.mpr ⟨k, hk, by simp [hc]⟩
  rw [h] at this
  cases this

/-- **Locality** (family 3): a change outside a fragment's support leaves its verdict. -/
theorem locality {Name Key V : Type} [DecidableEq Key] {f : Frag Name Key V} (hf : f.ReadsOnly)
    {changed : List Key} {w₁ w₂ : Key → V} (hout : ∀ k, k ∉ changed → w₁ k = w₂ k)
    (hna : f.affected changed = false) : f.check w₁ = f.check w₂ :=
  hf w₁ w₂ fun k hk => hout k (Frag.unaffected hna k hk)

/-- **Selective repair agrees with checking from scratch** (family 3): from correct verdicts for
`w₁`, re-checking only the fragments a change of `changed` affects gives exactly the verdicts a
full re-check of `w₂` gives. -/
theorem repair_agrees_from_scratch {Name Key V : Type} [DecidableEq Key]
    (fs : List (Frag Name Key V)) (hfs : ∀ f ∈ fs, f.ReadsOnly) {changed : List Key}
    {w₁ w₂ : Key → V} (hout : ∀ k, k ∉ changed → w₁ k = w₂ k) :
    repair fs (fromScratch fs w₁) changed w₂ = fromScratch fs w₂ := by
  induction fs with
  | nil => rfl
  | cons f fs ih =>
    simp only [fromScratch, List.map_cons, repair]
    have ih' := ih (fun g hg => hfs g (by simp [hg]))
    simp only [fromScratch] at ih'
    rw [ih']
    congr 1
    cases ha : f.affected changed with
    | true => rfl
    | false => exact locality (hfs f (by simp)) hout ha

/-- The explicit residual obligations of a repair are those of a full re-check. -/
theorem repair_residual {Name Key V : Type} [DecidableEq Key]
    (fs : List (Frag Name Key V)) (hfs : ∀ f ∈ fs, f.ReadsOnly) {changed : List Key}
    {w₁ w₂ : Key → V} (hout : ∀ k, k ∉ changed → w₁ k = w₂ k) :
    residual fs (repair fs (fromScratch fs w₁) changed w₂) = residual fs (fromScratch fs w₂) := by
  rw [repair_agrees_from_scratch fs hfs hout]

/-- **Repair reads only the affected fragments**: two new worlds on which every AFFECTED fragment
checks alike yield the same repair; the unaffected verdicts are reused, never recomputed. -/
theorem repair_reuses {Name Key V : Type} [DecidableEq Key] (fs : List (Frag Name Key V))
    (cache : List Bool) (hlen : cache.length = fs.length) (changed : List Key) {w w' : Key → V}
    (h : ∀ f ∈ fs, f.affected changed = true → f.check w = f.check w') :
    repair fs cache changed w = repair fs cache changed w' := by
  induction fs generalizing cache with
  | nil => rfl
  | cons f fs ih =>
    have ih' := fun c hc => ih c hc (fun g hg => h g (by simp [hg]))
    cases cache with
    | nil => cases hlen
    | cons c cs =>
      simp only [repair]
      rw [ih' cs (by simpa using hlen)]
      congr 1
      cases ha : f.affected changed with
      | true => simp [h f (by simp) ha]
      | false => rfl

/-! ## Representation change -/

theorem count_map_inj {α β : Type} [DecidableEq α] [DecidableEq β] {e : α → β} {e' : β → α}
    (h₁ : ∀ a, e' (e a) = a) (l : List α) (a : α) : (l.map e).count (e a) = l.count a := by
  induction l with
  | nil => rfl
  | cons x l ih =>
    simp only [List.map_cons, List.count_cons, ih]
    by_cases hx : x = a
    · subst hx; simp
    · have hex : e x ≠ e a := fun h => hx (by rw [← h₁ x, h, h₁])
      simp [hx, hex]

/-- Renaming along a map with a left inverse (injective) preserves bag inclusion. -/
theorem SubBag.map [DecidableEq Tok] {Tok' : Type} [DecidableEq Tok'] {e : Tok → Tok'}
    {e' : Tok' → Tok} (h₁ : ∀ a, e' (e a) = a) {Δ₁ Δ₂ : List Tok} (h : SubBag Δ₁ Δ₂) :
    SubBag (Δ₁.map e) (Δ₂.map e) := by
  intro b
  by_cases hb : ∃ a, e a = b
  · obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := hb
    rw [count_map_inj h₁, count_map_inj h₁]
    exact h a
  · have hn : b ∉ Δ₁.map e := fun hm => hb (by
      obtain ⟨a, _, ha⟩ := List.mem_map.mp hm
      exact ⟨a, ha⟩)
    rw [List.count_eq_zero.mpr hn]
    exact Nat.zero_le _

theorem map_erase_bij {α β : Type} [DecidableEq α] [DecidableEq β] {e : α → β} {e' : β → α}
    (h₁ : ∀ a, e' (e a) = a) (l : List α) (a : α) : (l.erase a).map e = (l.map e).erase (e a) := by
  induction l with
  | nil => rfl
  | cons x l ih =>
    by_cases hx : x = a
    · subst hx; simp
    · have hex : e x ≠ e a := fun h => hx (by rw [← h₁ x, h, h₁])
      simp [hx, hex, ih]

/-- **Representation change transports the judgment**: renaming every token along a checked
correspondence (a map with a left inverse, so possibly PARTIAL on the new side: stale
representations need not name anything) carries a judged protocol to a judged protocol over the
new representation, its tokens renamed. -/
theorem hasProt_mapTok {Tok' : Type} [DecidableEq Tok] [DecidableEq Tok']
    {e : Tok → Tok'} {e' : Tok' → Tok} (h₁ : ∀ a, e' (e a) = a)
    {sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob} {Ω : Ctx S Hole A Tok Fact Ob} {Γ : List Fact}
    {Q : (j : Ix) → A j → Prop} {Φ : List Ob} {Δ : List Tok} {i : Ix} {P : Prot S Hole A i}
    (h : HasProt sp Ω Γ Q Φ Δ P) : HasProt (sp.mapTok e) (Ω.mapTok e) Γ Q Φ (Δ.map e) P := by
  induction h with
  | ret a hq => exact .ret a hq
  | call op k hc hr he _ ih =>
    exact .call op k (by simp [Spec.mapTok, hc]) hr he ih
  | @spend Δ i op k t hc ht hr he _ ih =>
    refine .spend op k (e t) (by simp [Spec.mapTok, hc]) (List.mem_map_of_mem ht) hr he ?_
    intro r
    have := ih r
    rwa [map_erase_bij h₁] at this
  | hole h I hI hp hctx hneed hpost howes =>
    refine .hole h (I.mapTok e) (by simp [Ctx.mapTok, hI]) hp hctx ?_ hpost howes
    exact SubBag.map h₁ hneed

/-- **Representation change transports admission**: an effect is admissible over the renamed
tokens, against the view read back through the correspondence, exactly when it was before. -/
theorem admitOp_mapTok {Tok' : Type} {e : Tok → Tok'} {e' : Tok' → Tok}
    (h₁ : ∀ a, e' (e a) = a) (sp : Spec S Tok Fact Ob) (v : View Tok Fact) {i : Ix}
    (op : S.Op i) :
    admitOp (sp.mapTok e) ⟨v.holds, fun b => v.live (e' b)⟩ op = admitOp sp v op := by
  unfold admitOp Spec.mapTok
  cases hc : sp.consumes op <;> simp [hc, h₁]

end

/-! ## Shared parameters -/

/-- **Separate witnesses are insufficient** (doc 2 section 4), a SCALAR ILLUSTRATION with `θ` a
price: each party's condition has a witness, and the completion space is empty:
`(∃x B x) ∧ (∃x S x) ⇏ ∃x (B x ∧ S x)`. The form over substitutions of an open protocol is
`Negotiation.separate_witnesses_over_substitutions`. -/
theorem separate_witnesses_insufficient :
    (∃ x, priceConds.guards x) ∧ (∃ x, priceConds.authority x) ∧ ¬ ∃ x, priceConds.space x := by
  refine ⟨⟨5, Nat.le_refl 5⟩, ⟨7, Nat.le_refl 7⟩, ?_⟩
  rintro ⟨x, _, hb, hs, _⟩
  have hb' : x ≤ 5 := hb
  have hs' : 7 ≤ x := hs
  omega

/-- The general form: per-condition witnesses never compose into a completion. -/
theorem witnesses_do_not_compose :
    ¬ ∀ (B S : Nat → Prop), (∃ x, B x) → (∃ x, S x) → ∃ x, B x ∧ S x := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨x, hb, hs⟩ := h priceConds.guards priceConds.authority
    separate_witnesses_insufficient.1 separate_witnesses_insufficient.2.1
  exact separate_witnesses_insufficient.2.2 ⟨x, trivial, hb, hs, trivial⟩

/-- The same instance, decided over a bounded price range. -/
theorem separate_witnesses_bounded :
    (∃ x : Fin 20, x.val ≤ 5) ∧ (∃ x : Fin 20, 7 ≤ x.val) ∧ ¬ ∃ x : Fin 20, x.val ≤ 5 ∧ 7 ≤ x.val := by
  decide

/-! ## Search state versus logical status -/

/-- **Greedy versus logical** (doc 2 section 4, the matcher), an ILLUSTRATION over number lists,
not over protocols: offers `[100, 50]`, wants `[50, 100]`:
first-fit satisfies one want of two, while a complete assignment (want 0 ← offer 1, want 1 ← offer
0) exists and complete search finds it. -/
theorem greedy_vs_logical :
    firstFit [100, 50] [50, 100] = 1 ∧ coverAll [100, 50] [50, 100] = true ∧
      Assigns [100, 50] [50, 100] [1, 0] := by
  refine ⟨by decide, by decide, ?_⟩
  unfold Assigns
  decide

/-- **Search state is not logical status**: a greedy shortfall does not refute the intent. -/
theorem search_state_ne_logical_status :
    ¬ ∀ offers wants : List Nat, firstFit offers wants < wants.length →
      ¬ ∃ picks, Assigns offers wants picks := by
  intro h
  exact h [100, 50] [50, 100] (by decide) ⟨[1, 0], greedy_vs_logical.2.2⟩

/-! ## A hole is not an interaction (doc 2 section 5) -/

namespace Coin

/-- Running the open plan under a filling: the filling's answer, compared with the peer's bit. -/
theorem wins_planHole (θ : Subst sig HoleN Res) (b : Bool) :
    wins b (subst θ planHole) () =
      match θ .revealed () with
      | some (.ret c) => c == b
      | _ => false := by
  have e : wins b (subst θ planHole) () =
      wins b (subst θ (Prot.hole (S := sig) (A := Res) (i := Phase.revealed) ())) () := rfl
  rw [e]
  cases hθ : θ .revealed () with
  | none => simp only [subst, hθ]; rfl
  | some f =>
    cases f with
    | ret c => simp only [subst, hθ]; rfl
    | call op k => exact nomatch op
    | hole h => simp only [subst, hθ]; rfl

/-- **No foresight, for a response-free naming**: `planHole` names its hole `()` in BOTH branches of
the peer's bit. For every environment SOME filling wins (`∀ E ∃ θ, Success (P[θ], E)`), but no
single filling wins against every environment (`¬ ∃ θ ∀ E`): the "commit a bit before you reveal
yours" game. This holds BECAUSE of the naming: with names that depend on the response the opposite
holds (`response_indexed_names_have_foresight`), and `foresight_iff_names_separate` is the exact
condition. Scope (one filling into every branch unchanged) is a naming discipline, not a fact of
the calculus. -/
theorem no_foresight :
    (∀ b, ∃ θ, wins b (subst θ planHole) () = true) ∧
      ¬ ∃ θ, ∀ b, wins b (subst θ planHole) () = true := by
  refine ⟨fun b => ⟨answer b, by rw [wins_planHole]; cases b <;> rfl⟩, ?_⟩
  rintro ⟨θ, hθ⟩
  have h0 := hθ false
  have h1 := hθ true
  rw [wins_planHole] at h0 h1
  cases hr : θ .revealed () with
  | none => simp [hr] at h0
  | some f =>
    cases f with
    | ret c => cases c <;> simp [hr] at h0 h1
    | call op k => exact nomatch op
    | hole h => simp [hr] at h0

/-- **The response-dependent continuation succeeds**: the same game with the answer written as
the continuation of the `call` (a family over the response) wins against every environment. -/
theorem response_dependent_succeeds : ∀ b, wins b planCall () = true := by
  intro b; cases b <;> rfl

/-- Running a named template under a filling: the filling of branch `b`'s hole, compared with `b`. -/
theorem wins_planNamed {Hn : Phase → Type} (name : Bool → Hn .revealed) (θ : Subst sig Hn Res)
    (b : Bool) :
    wins b (subst θ (planNamed name)) () =
      match θ .revealed (name b) with
      | some (.ret c) => c == b
      | _ => false := by
  have e : wins b (subst θ (planNamed name)) () =
      wins b (subst θ (Prot.hole (S := sig) (A := Res) (i := Phase.revealed) (name b))) () := rfl
  rw [e]
  cases hθ : θ .revealed (name b) with
  | none => simp only [subst, hθ]; rfl
  | some f =>
    cases f with
    | ret c => simp only [subst, hθ]; rfl
    | call op k => exact nomatch op
    | hole h => simp only [subst, hθ]; rfl

/-- **Foresight exactly when the names separate**: a single filling chosen before the reveal wins
against every bit iff the template gives the two branches DIFFERENT hole names. A response-free
naming (`name true = name false`) leaves no causal strategy; a response-indexed one is a filling
per response. -/
theorem foresight_iff_names_separate {Hn : Phase → Type} [DecidableEq (Hn .revealed)]
    (name : Bool → Hn .revealed) :
    (∃ θ : Subst sig Hn Res, ∀ b, wins b (subst θ (planNamed name)) () = true) ↔
      name true ≠ name false := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨θ, hθ⟩ heq
    have h0 := hθ false
    have h1 := hθ true
    rw [wins_planNamed] at h0 h1
    rw [heq] at h1
    cases hr : θ .revealed (name false) with
    | none => simp [hr] at h0
    | some f =>
      cases f with
      | ret c => cases c <;> simp [hr] at h0 h1
      | call op k => exact nomatch op
      | hole h => simp [hr] at h0
  · intro hne
    refine ⟨fun i => match i with
      | .waiting => fun _ => none
      | .revealed => fun n => some (.ret (decide (n = name true))), fun b => ?_⟩
    rw [wins_planNamed]
    cases b with
    | true => simp
    | false => simp [Ne.symm hne]

/-- **Response-indexed names have foresight**: `call recv (fun b => hole b)` (one hole name per bit,
well typed) admits ONE filling that wins against every environment. A hole whose name depends on the
response is a family over the response, exactly like a `call` continuation. -/
theorem response_indexed_names_have_foresight :
    ∃ θ : Subst sig HoleB Res, ∀ b, wins b (subst θ (planNamed (Hn := HoleB) fun b => b)) () = true :=
  (@foresight_iff_names_separate HoleB (inferInstanceAs (DecidableEq Bool)) fun b => b).mpr
    (by intro h; cases h)

/-- `planHole` is the response-free naming. -/
theorem planHole_named : planHole = planNamed (Hn := HoleN) fun _ => () := rfl

/-- **A `theirs` hole is never planned**: declared `theirs`, the hole is never filled by our plan, so
every run of the open plan stops at the hole. It "loses" only because `wins` scores a stuck run as
`false`: the theorem says the planner cannot win by filling, not that the peer wins. -/
theorem theirs_never_planned (σ : Subst sig HoleN Res) (b : Bool) :
    wins b (fill (ctxOf .theirs) σ planHole) () = false := by
  unfold fill
  rw [wins_planHole]
  simp [Subst.ours, ctxOf, iface]

end Coin

/-! ## Nano's free program over effects is an open protocol with a trivial index and no holes

`Hosting.Resident.Prog` (`cmd | keep | forget | ask | say`, a continuation per result) is the
instance `Ix := Unit`, `Hole := Empty` (the embedding is `Lang.Contextual.NanoBridge`). -/

namespace Nano

open Nanodregg.Hosting Nanodregg.Hosting.Resident

theorem runs_of_nano {α : Type} {p : Prog α} {es : List Ev} {a : α}
    (h : Proofs.ResidentRun.Runs p es a) : ∃ tr, Runs (ofProg p) tr () a ∧ tr.map toEv = es := by
  induction h with
  | done a => exact ⟨[], Runs.ret (S := sig) (Hole := fun _ => Empty) (A := fun _ => α) (i := ()) a, rfl⟩
  | @cmd c k es a x _ ih =>
    obtain ⟨tr, h, e⟩ := ih
    exact ⟨⟨(), NOp.cmd c, x⟩ :: tr, Runs.call (S := sig) (op := NOp.cmd c) x h, by simp [toEv, e]⟩
  | @keep r t k es a b _ ih =>
    obtain ⟨tr, h, e⟩ := ih
    exact ⟨⟨(), NOp.keep r t, b⟩ :: tr, Runs.call (S := sig) (op := NOp.keep r t) b h,
      by simp [toEv, e]⟩
  | @forget k es a b _ ih =>
    obtain ⟨tr, h, e⟩ := ih
    exact ⟨⟨(), NOp.forget, b⟩ :: tr, Runs.call (S := sig) (op := NOp.forget) b h,
      by simp [toEv, e]⟩
  | @ask r q k es a x _ ih =>
    obtain ⟨tr, h, e⟩ := ih
    exact ⟨⟨(), NOp.ask r q, x⟩ :: tr, Runs.call (S := sig) (op := NOp.ask r q) x h,
      by simp [toEv, e]⟩
  | @say s k es a _ ih =>
    obtain ⟨tr, h, e⟩ := ih
    exact ⟨⟨(), NOp.say s, ()⟩ :: tr, Runs.call (S := sig) (op := NOp.say s) () h,
      by simp [toEv, e]⟩

theorem nano_of_runs {α : Type} (p : Prog α) {tr : Trace sig} {a : α}
    (h : Runs (ofProg p) tr () a) : Proofs.ResidentRun.Runs p (tr.map toEv) a := by
  induction p generalizing tr with
  | done b =>
    cases h
    exact .done _
  | cmd c k ih =>
    cases h with
    | call x h => exact .cmd x (ih x h)
  | keep r t k ih =>
    cases h with
    | call b h => exact .keep b (ih b h)
  | forget k ih =>
    cases h with
    | call b h => exact .forget b (ih b h)
  | ask r q k ih =>
    cases h with
    | call x h => exact .ask x (ih x h)
  | say s k ih =>
    cases h with
    | call u h => exact .say (ih h)

/-- **Nano's paths are protocol paths**: `Hosting.Proofs.ResidentRun.Runs p es a` is exactly a
`Runs` path of the protocol `ofProg p`, read through `toEv`. -/
theorem nano_runs_iff {α : Type} (p : Prog α) (es : List Ev) (a : α) :
    Proofs.ResidentRun.Runs p es a ↔ ∃ tr, Runs (ofProg p) tr () a ∧ tr.map toEv = es :=
  ⟨runs_of_nano, fun ⟨_, h, e⟩ => e ▸ nano_of_runs p h⟩

/-- **The interpreters agree**: nano's `Prog.interp` at its recording handler computes what this
module's `interpret` computes at the recording oracle environment: the same value, the same
counter, and the trace read through `toEv`. -/
theorem nano_interp_agrees (o : Oracle) {α : Type} (p : Prog α) (n : Nat) (es : List Ev)
    (tr₀ : Trace sig) :
    ∃ a n' tr, interpret (record (oracleH o)) (ofProg p) (n, tr₀) = .done () a (n', tr₀ ++ tr) ∧
      (p.interp (recorder o)).run (n, es) = (a, (n', es ++ tr.map toEv)) := by
  induction p generalizing n es tr₀ with
  | done a => exact ⟨a, n, [], by simp [interpret, fold, execAlgebra, ofProg], by simp [Prog.interp]; rfl⟩
  | cmd c k ih =>
    obtain ⟨a, n', tr, h1, h2⟩ := ih (o.cmd n) (n + 1) (es ++ [.cmd c (o.cmd n)])
      (tr₀ ++ [⟨(), NOp.cmd c, o.cmd n⟩])
    exact ⟨a, n', ⟨(), NOp.cmd c, o.cmd n⟩ :: tr, by simpa [interpret, fold, execAlgebra, record, ofProg, oracleH] using h1,
      by simpa [Prog.interp, recorder, toEv] using h2⟩
  | keep r t k ih =>
    obtain ⟨a, n', tr, h1, h2⟩ := ih (o.keep n) (n + 1) (es ++ [.keep r t (o.keep n)])
      (tr₀ ++ [⟨(), NOp.keep r t, o.keep n⟩])
    exact ⟨a, n', ⟨(), NOp.keep r t, o.keep n⟩ :: tr, by simpa [interpret, fold, execAlgebra, record, ofProg, oracleH] using h1,
      by simpa [Prog.interp, recorder, toEv] using h2⟩
  | forget k ih =>
    obtain ⟨a, n', tr, h1, h2⟩ := ih (o.forget n) (n + 1) (es ++ [.forget (o.forget n)])
      (tr₀ ++ [⟨(), NOp.forget, o.forget n⟩])
    exact ⟨a, n', ⟨(), NOp.forget, o.forget n⟩ :: tr, by simpa [interpret, fold, execAlgebra, record, ofProg, oracleH] using h1,
      by simpa [Prog.interp, recorder, toEv] using h2⟩
  | ask r q k ih =>
    obtain ⟨a, n', tr, h1, h2⟩ := ih (o.ask n) (n + 1) (es ++ [.ask r q (o.ask n)])
      (tr₀ ++ [⟨(), NOp.ask r q, o.ask n⟩])
    exact ⟨a, n', ⟨(), NOp.ask r q, o.ask n⟩ :: tr, by simpa [interpret, fold, execAlgebra, record, ofProg, oracleH] using h1,
      by simpa [Prog.interp, recorder, toEv] using h2⟩
  | say s k ih =>
    obtain ⟨a, n', tr, h1, h2⟩ := ih (n + 1) (es ++ [.say s]) (tr₀ ++ [⟨(), NOp.say s, ()⟩])
    exact ⟨a, n', ⟨(), NOp.say s, ()⟩ :: tr, by simpa [interpret, fold, execAlgebra, record, ofProg, oracleH] using h1,
      by simpa [Prog.interp, recorder, toEv] using h2⟩

/-- **`interp_runs`, recovered**: nano's theorem (the interpreter performs exactly a path, for
every oracle) follows from this module's `interpret_record`, the agreement of the interpreters,
and `nano_runs_iff`. -/
theorem nano_interp_runs (o : Oracle) {α : Type} (p : Prog α) (n : Nat) (es : List Ev) :
    ∃ es', ((p.interp (recorder o)).run (n, es)).2.2 = es ++ es' ∧
      Proofs.ResidentRun.Runs p es' ((p.interp (recorder o)).run (n, es)).1 := by
  obtain ⟨a, n', tr, h1, h2⟩ := nano_interp_agrees o p n es []
  have hr := interpret_record (oracleH o) (ofProg p) n []
  rw [h1] at hr
  obtain ⟨tr', htr, hrun⟩ := hr
  simp only [List.nil_append] at htr
  subst htr
  rw [h2]
  exact ⟨tr.map toEv, rfl, nano_of_runs p hrun⟩

end Nano

